 "title": "Choose many, where the data has groups",
 "caption": "It stands in a rail, the navigation and the content attached, at the body's full width: the rail is open at a desktop and shut to its icons on a tablet, and on a phone one bar stands at the top. The choices are saved once, so the page is one container, and its header is the page level: the way back, the kind the choices are for, and a line under it. Its actions stand at the start of its footer. The groups come from the data, so each is a part of the content under its own title, with a line above it. The choices stand in columns: each column starts at the same place in every row and in every group, so a person reads down a column as well as along a row. A row with fewer choices leaves its last places empty. Every screen shows every group and every choice. They stand four across at a desktop and on a tablet, and on a phone one under another.",
